# Cloudflare Workers static-assets redirects (copied to build/_redirects by Docusaurus).
#
# /privacy is the canonical privacy policy. /docs/privacy was a second, separately
# maintained copy of the same document under the docs sidebar; the two drifted (different
# last-updated dates, different sections) and both the footer and the docs sidebar pointed
# at the stale one. The duplicate is retired rather than kept in sync — a legal document
# with two texts is worse than one, and App Store Connect must name exactly one URL.
/docs/privacy          /privacy           301
/zh-Hans/docs/privacy  /zh-Hans/privacy   301

# /support is quoted as a support URL but has never existed; /contact is the real support
# page and returns 200. Redirect rather than ship a 404.
/support               /contact           301
/zh-Hans/support       /zh-Hans/contact   301

# trailingSlash: true since 2026-09-04 means the URLs Google remembers (old sitemap, old
# inlinks) carry a trailing slash, and the rules above match only the bare form: Googlebot
# 404'd /docs/privacy/ daily for a week (ud task 70775310). The slashed forms redirect to the
# same successors. /docs/category/deployment was the auto-generated category page that vanished
# when the deployment docs were merged into /docs/self-deployment/ (fc25b94); it never had a rule.
/docs/privacy/                     /privacy                    301
/zh-Hans/docs/privacy/             /zh-Hans/privacy            301
/support/                          /contact                    301
/zh-Hans/support/                  /zh-Hans/contact            301
/docs/category/deployment          /docs/self-deployment/      301
/docs/category/deployment/         /docs/self-deployment/      301
/zh-Hans/docs/category/deployment  /zh-Hans/docs/self-deployment/  301
/zh-Hans/docs/category/deployment/ /zh-Hans/docs/self-deployment/  301

# /subscribe was the pricing page until 2026-09-19; the owner kept exactly one pricing
# page, /docs/pricing/, and this one was retired. Both slash forms, both locales.
/subscribe                 /docs/pricing/           301
/subscribe/                /docs/pricing/           301
/zh-Hans/subscribe         /zh-Hans/docs/pricing/   301
/zh-Hans/subscribe/        /zh-Hans/docs/pricing/   301

# Paths are case-sensitive on Workers Static Assets: /zh-hans/... is a 404, and the 404 page
# still fires the RUM beacon, which is how four readers were seen landing on lowercase
# /zh-hans/ URLs in one day (2026-09-24, ud task 2cb63040) with no referer to say where the
# links came from. Fold the lowercase locale prefix back onto the real one, path preserved.
# Only the all-lowercase form is covered; it is the only form that has been observed.
/zh-hans        /zh-Hans/        301
/zh-hans/*      /zh-Hans/:splat  301
